# LUXORA — Full-Stack Development Plan

## Current Stack
- Frontend: React + Vite (deployed on Vercel)
- Backend: Node.js + Express
- Database: lowdb (JSON file)
- Auth: JWT
- Currency: Live exchange rates

---

## Phase 1 — Real Database (MongoDB + Mongoose)
**Goal:** Replace lowdb with MongoDB Atlas

- [ ] Set up MongoDB Atlas free cluster
- [ ] Install mongoose in backend
- [ ] Create models: User, Product, Order, OrderItem
- [ ] Migrate all routes to use Mongoose
- [ ] Update .env with MONGODB_URI
- [ ] Seed products into MongoDB

---

## Phase 2 — Products on the Backend
**Goal:** Move products from frontend JS file to MongoDB

- [ ] Seed all 50 frontend products into MongoDB
- [ ] Create full products API (CRUD)
- [ ] Update frontend to fetch products from API
- [ ] Remove hardcoded products.js dependency
- [ ] Add search and filter on the backend

---

## Phase 3 — Admin Dashboard Backend
**Goal:** Wire existing admin UI to the backend

- [ ] Admin: add/edit/delete products (persisted in MongoDB)
- [ ] Admin: view all orders
- [ ] Admin: update order status (pending → processing → shipped → delivered)
- [ ] Protect admin routes with role-based middleware
- [ ] Frontend admin panel reads/writes from API

---

## Phase 4 — Stripe Payment Integration
**Goal:** Replace mock payment with real Stripe checkout

- [ ] Set up Stripe account + API keys
- [ ] Install stripe package in backend
- [ ] Create payment intent endpoint
- [ ] Add Stripe card element to checkout modal
- [ ] Confirm payment before saving order
- [ ] Handle webhooks for payment confirmation

---

## Phase 5 — Deploy Everything
**Goal:** Live URL for submission

- [ ] Deploy backend to Railway or Render
- [ ] Set environment variables on hosting platform
- [ ] Connect frontend to deployed backend URL
- [ ] Deploy frontend to Vercel
- [ ] Test full flow on live URL
- [ ] Update README with live links

